<h2 id="faq-heading">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<div class="usa-accordion usa-accordion--bordered usa-accordion--multiselectable" data-allow-multiple="">
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="faq-1">How much does a conveyor system cost?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-1" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Conveyor costs depend on seven factors: type, length/width, frame material, motor/drive, controls, environment, and installation. Gravity <a href="/conveyor-types/roller-conveyors/">roller conveyors</a> are the least expensive. Fully automated systems with servo drives and <a href="/industries/food-conveyors/sanitary/">sanitary stainless steel</a> construction are the most expensive. Get 2–3 manufacturer quotes with a detailed specification to compare accurately.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-2">What is the most expensive part of a conveyor system?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-2" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Controls and automation typically account for 15–40% of total cost on <a href="/resources/automated-conveyor-systems/">automated conveyor systems</a>. This includes the PLC, HMI, VFDs, servo drives, sensors, control panels, wiring, and programming. For simple conveyors, the frame and drive components dominate cost. For sanitary environments, stainless steel construction adds 50–100% over carbon steel.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-3">Why do conveyor prices vary so much between quotes?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-3" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Quote variation stems from scope differences, materials (carbon steel vs stainless), controls scope (motor starter vs PLC package), motor quality, design engineering time, warranty terms, and installation services. A detailed specification document ensures all vendors bid on the same scope. Use the "Questions to Ask Manufacturers" checklist above to identify scope differences between quotes.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-4">What questions should I ask conveyor manufacturers?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-4" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Ask about controls scope (what's included vs. excluded), frame and belt materials, lead time, installation services, commissioning duration, warranty coverage (parts vs. parts + labor), wear part costs, energy consumption, and future expansion capability. See the full 18-question checklist above for the complete list.</p>

</div>
